    [
     1,
     "How wonderful! I can&#39;t wait to use the stamen maps in particular.\r<br>Thank you David and Hadley both for putting this together.\r<br>\r<br>However, the line at the top where you say &quot;Two cool images from ggmap\r<br>are available here&quot; .. the link doesn&#39;t show for me. Please could you\r<br>re-post?\r<br>\r<br>many thanks, Andrew\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Apr 13, 12:54 pm, David Kahle &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">david.ka...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Just uploaded; should be available shortly.  In particular, the bug referenced in several list emails has been addressed.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Two cool images from ggmap are available here.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Happy mapping!\r<br>&gt; david.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; ggmap 2.0\r<br>&gt; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; NEW FEATURES\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * a vast array of new kinds of maps are available to the user.  these are based on stamen maps (<a href=\"http://maps.stamen.com/watercolor/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://maps.stamen.com/watercolor/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191106000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZCeON4y7S2FMoowb1A-F4\">http://maps.stamen.com/watercolor/</a>) and cloudmade maps (<a href=\"http://maps.cloudmade.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://maps.cloudmade.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191106000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0SSuslAeyDUrBZyCRMTSFv\">http://maps.cloudmade.com/</a>).  the latter allows for user-designed map rendering (<a href=\"http://maps.cloudmade.com/editor#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://maps.cloudmade.com/editor%23&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191106000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OKWeNfO6H9ui7RlF8pH2L\">http://maps.cloudmade.com/editor#</a>).\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * the full google static maps api is available to the user.  in particular, this allows for double the image resolution of google maps (which is also now the default).\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * qmplot - a version of qplot (from ggplot2) which automatically determines, downloads, and plots the result on the appropriate map.  this function is still experimental.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * make_bbox - a function which determines an appropriate bounding box for a collection of longitude/latitude pairs.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; CHANGES\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * ggmap now imports all packages save ggplot2 instead of depending on them.\r<br>&gt; * ggmapplot no longer uses a textConnection for parsing base_layer.\r<br>&gt; * geocode fixes/changes :\r<br>&gt;         a. gcdf is no longer a global variable\r<br>&gt;         b. geocode now properly uses the google geocoding api (like revgeocode)\r<br>&gt;         c. geocodeQueryCheck watches your query limit with hidden global variable .GoogleGeocodeQueryCount\r<br>&gt; * verbose argument in function ggmap now deprecated, use messaging\r<br>&gt; * center argument in function ggmap now deprecated, use location\r<br>&gt; * the ggmap function has been totally overhauled.  it is no longer based on the RgoogleMaps functions GetMap and GetMap.OSM but on functions get_googlemap, get_openstreetmap, get_stamenmap, and get_cloudmademap.\r<br>&gt; * ggimage has been rebased on ggmap:::geom_raster (a version of ggplot2&#39;s geom_raster which smooths).\r<br>&gt; * ggmap&#39;s version of annotation_raster and annotation_custom are now exported as inset_raster and inset.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; FUNCTION NAME CHANGES\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * the function called ggmap in previous versions is now called get_map.\r<br>&gt; * the function called ggmapplot in previous versions is now called ggmap.  the new ggmap function checks its arguments and then either 1. proceeds with generating a ggplot2 object or 2. errors suggesting the use of get_map.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; FIXES\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * bug was fixed which on some platforms caused an error in readPNG.\r<br>&gt; * mapdist now properly handles many from queries without exceeding google&#39;s distance matrix api uri limits.  note that the api may still reject large queries - you may want to run mapdist in a for loop.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; NEW DEPENDS/IMPORTS/SUGGESTS\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * ggmap no longer imports ReadImages.\r<br>&gt; * ggmap now suggests stringr.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; OTHER ADDITIONS\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; * a new data set on wind from hurricane ike (from NOAA).\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; -------------------------------------------------------------\r<br>&gt; -------------------------------------------------------------\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; David J. Kahle, Ph.D.\r<br>&gt; Assistant Professor of Statistical Science\r<br>&gt; Department of Statistical Science\r<br>&gt; Baylor University\r<br>&gt; One Bear Place #97140\r<br>&gt; Waco, Texas 76798\r<br>&gt; Office : <a href=\"tel:(254)%20710-6102\" value=\"+12547106102\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(254) 710-6102</a><a href=\"http://sites.google.com/site/davidkahle/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sites.google.com/site/davidkahle/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191106000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0peUAaIc3HizFygBDLyvif\">http://sites.google.com/site/davidkahle/</a>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "SVRCgbkcjNIJ",
   "from": "David Kahle",
   "author": "e4aec126ff1dca22",
   "date": "2012-04-16T00:39:31Z",
   "subject": "Re: ggmap 2.0 uploaded to CRAN",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>Thanks, Andrew!  And thanks as well to all those who have emailed me directly, it&#39;s been great to get such a positive reception.<div><br></div><div>A number of you have asked for some more examples/help.  I&#39;m attaching (via Dropbox) a draft of the paper Hadley and I are working on for ggmap, it goes over most of the capabilities of the package and discusses some future directions.  I&#39;d love to hear any feedback you have on it!  Otherwise, if nothing else hopefully you&#39;ll enjoy the pretty pictures. :)</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>david.</div><div><br></div></div><div><a href=\"http://dl.dropbox.com/u/24648660/RJwrapper.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dl.dropbox.com/u/24648660/RJwrapper.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191110000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20_nwxT5LqJxnknv5PzGQL\">http://dl.dropbox.com/u/24648660/RJwrapper.pdf</a></div><div><br></div><div><br><div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div>On Apr 15, 2012, at 11:07 AM, wooster wrote:</div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>How wonderful! I can&#39;t wait to use the stamen maps in particular.<br>Thank you David and Hadley both for putting this together.<br><br>However, the line at the top where you say &quot;Two cool images from ggmap<br>are available here&quot; .. the link doesn&#39;t show for me. Please could you<br>re-post?<br><br>many thanks, Andrew<br><br>On Apr 13, 12:54 pm, David Kahle &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">david.ka...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><blockquote type=\"cite\">Just uploaded; should be available shortly.  In particular, the bug referenced in several list emails has been addressed.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">Two cool images from ggmap are available here.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">Happy mapping!<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">david.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">ggmap 2.0<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">-------------------------------------------------------------------------<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">NEW FEATURES<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* a vast array of new kinds of maps are available to the user.  these are based on stamen maps (<a href=\"http://maps.stamen.com/watercolor/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://maps.stamen.com/watercolor/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191110000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JoJUH0_ljFtzmDvXZwzCZ\">http://maps.stamen.com/watercolor/</a>) and cloudmade maps (<a href=\"http://maps.cloudmade.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://maps.cloudmade.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191110000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LtBHWwGIYnqAjJjZDqePZ\">http://maps.cloudmade.com/</a>).  the latter allows for user-designed map rendering (<a href=\"http://maps.cloudmade.com/editor#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://maps.cloudmade.com/editor%23&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376191110000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38q84izXrCPgsvlTRPRm-o\">http://maps.cloudmade.com/editor#</a>).<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* the full google static maps api is available to the user.  in particular, this allows for double the image resolution of google maps (which is also now the default).<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* qmplot - a version of qplot (from ggplot2) which automatically determines, downloads, and plots the result on the appropriate map.  this function is still experimental.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* make_bbox - a function which determines an appropriate bounding box for a collection of longitude/latitude pairs.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">CHANGES<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* ggmap now imports all packages save ggplot2 instead of depending on them.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* ggmapplot no longer uses a textConnection for parsing base_layer.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* geocode fixes/changes :<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">        a. gcdf is no longer a global variable<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">        b. geocode now properly uses the google geocoding api (like revgeocode)<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">        c. geocodeQueryCheck watches your query limit with hidden global variable .GoogleGeocodeQueryCount<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* verbose argument in function ggmap now deprecated, use messaging<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* center argument in function ggmap now deprecated, use location<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* the ggmap function has been totally overhauled.  it is no longer based on the RgoogleMaps functions GetMap and GetMap.OSM but on functions get_googlemap, get_openstreetmap, get_stamenmap, and get_cloudmademap.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* ggimage has been rebased on ggmap:::geom_raster (a version of ggplot2&#39;s geom_raster which smooths).<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* ggmap&#39;s version of annotation_raster and annotation_custom are now exported as inset_raster and inset.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">FUNCTION NAME CHANGES<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* the function called ggmap in previous versions is now called get_map.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* the function called ggmapplot in previous versions is now called ggmap.  the new ggmap function checks its arguments and then either 1. proceeds with generating a ggplot2 object or 2. errors suggesting the use of get_map.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">FIXES<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* bug was fixed which on some platforms caused an error in readPNG.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* mapdist now properly handles many from queries without exceeding google&#39;s distance matrix api uri limits.  note that the api may still reject large queries - you may want to run mapdist in a for loop.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">NEW DEPENDS/IMPORTS/SUGGESTS<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* ggmap no longer imports ReadImages.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* ggmap now suggests stringr.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">OTHER ADDITIONS<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">* a new data set on wind from hurricane ike (from NOAA).<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">-------------------------------------------------------------<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">-------------------------------------------------------------<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\"><br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">David J. Kahle, Ph.D.<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">Assistant Professor of Statistical Science<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">Department of Statistical Science<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">Baylor University<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">One Bear Place #97140<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">Waco, Texas 76798<br></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\">Office : (254) <a rel=\"nofollow\">710-6102http://sites.google.com/site/davidkahle/</a><br></blockquote><br></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
